# Networking Task

Task: Create a network bridge named `{{bridge_name}}` that uses a dummy interface named `{{dummy_if}}` as its only port.

- The bridge `{{bridge_name}}` must exist, be up, and have the address `{{bridge_ip}}` configured.
- The dummy interface `{{dummy_if}}` must exist and be enslaved to `{{bridge_name}}`.
- The `dummy` kernel module must be loaded automatically at boot through a file in `/etc/modules-load.d/`.
- Make the bridge and its port persistent using new dedicated configuration files; do not overwrite or delete any existing network configuration files.
- Do not modify any physical network interface or the system default route.
- The configuration must persist across reboots.
